sub:assertion {
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/thompson1917-ch06-02> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/Claim>;
    dc:description "Skeletal spicules, as in sponges and radiolaria, are characteristically deposited in the interfacial boundaries between cells or vacuoles, and their form is in many cases regulated by the arrangement of these boundaries.";
    dc:type "empirical-generalization";
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Spicules are deposited at interfaces between cells or vacuoles";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/context> "D’Arcy Wentworth Thompson, On Growth and Form (1st ed., Cambridge: Cambridge University Press, 1917), Chapter VI, “A Note on Adsorption”; topic “Adsorption and membrane formation”. Scope: spicule-forming organisms, especially sponges and radiolaria"
}
